  "checks": [
    "Capture copies descriptor values and retains all five texture slots under one graphics lease; the underlying texture pixels remain shared. The source material may change or close before the snapshot is queried.",
    "A snapshot records the creator thread. Missing slots return null. Acquiring a texture yields an independent owner that outlives the snapshot.",
    "Native and language fixtures verify source replacement, duplicate texture identity, aliases, and engine Busy. Native fixtures verify allocation failure and foreign-thread rejection. In a live GL context, injected reference saturation verifies full capture rollback, and injected foreign context identity verifies checked close retry without consuming any references.",
    "Generated language code calls capture, settings, and texture acquisition directly. Across 128 paired capture/query/close operations, handwritten C makes 128 allocations and xlang makes 384. Reads alone make no allocations in either version. These counts do not measure elapsed time.",
    "Both platforms pass JIT, dynamic AOT, static AOT, import checks, and the material snapshot example. Native C fixtures pass O0/O2 with host and static XGE."
